From 1db18d13f7218d7034c40998be2d6ab3613798d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaxdad <atxhxag@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:48:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(egfx): let an H.264 decoder present frames itself

A decoder can now show AVC pictures itself instead of returning them to
the client-side compositor, for example a browser client whose hardware
decoder draws straight onto a canvas and cannot return pixels
synchronously.

Such a decoder answers true from `H264Decoder::presents_frames` and
receives each AVC420 frame, with its region rectangles, through
`H264Decoder::present`; the compositor does not paint those regions. AVC444
is advertised for it too: both views go to the decoder in order, because
they share one H.264 stream, and only the main view, an ordinary 4:2:0
picture, is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
